  <static seed="204" source="Contrib/DMOI/2-Sequences/2_3-Polynomial_Fitting/2_3_2.pg">
    <statement><p>Use polynomial fitting to find the formula for the <m>n</m>th term of the sequence <m>(a_n)_{n \ge 0}</m> which starts,</p>
<p><m>{-1, 2, 7, 14, 23, 34}, \ldots</m></p>
<p><m>a_n =</m> <fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>n^{2}+2n-1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>a_n = {n^{2}+2n-1}\text{.}</m> Here we know that we are looking for a quadratic because the second differences are constant. So <m>a_n = an^2 + bn + c\text{.}</m> Since <m>a_0 = {-1}</m>, we know <m>c= {-1}\text{.}</m> So just solve the system</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}
{2} \amp  = a + b + {-1}\\
{7} \amp  = 4a + 2b + {-1}
\end{aligned}</m></p>
<p>to find <m>a = {1}</m> and <m>b = {2}</m>.</p>
</solution>
